Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-26-2001||12:40 AM||||I'm soooo sorry to post another kill story, but this one is wierd!  Remember that Dude in the twin-turbo RX7 that I raced in my SE?  Well, I was cruizing in my GT when I pulled up along side of him again.  Since I was driving a different car last time, I thought I'd roll down my window and say "hi."  I think he's was a little confused to see my driving another GOLD fiero.  Anyways, his buddy in a 2nd gen Honda CRX was following him closely.  This CRX had the typical riceboy gear... fart pipe, 17in rims, etc... But this one was yellow and rusty as hell!  I was like: "why does a person spend the $ for nice 17in. rims on a rusty honda?" So at the next light, the CRX goes completely out of his way to line up next to my GT.  And wouldn't you know, he wants to race.  We were sitting on a slight incline and he was working the clutch to stay still.  The funny part was that he was revving his engine to at least 4,000 rpm and moving back and forth about 1/2 a car length to stay even at the light...  This guy obviously can't drive stick! No peds or traffic in front of us, so I edge forward in my nearly stock auto GT to show my intent.  Right before the light goes green, he revvs the living sh!t out of his car.  I 1/2 expected to lose(knowing that my auto GT isn't exactly a powerhouse and he's got a manual tranny, but I thought it might be intersting since my GT did really well against a more "tasefully" done civic."  Anyhow, after all that racket he only chrips his tires on the launch.  I put the GT to the wood and wait for him to pass me.   Not only did he lose, but he lost badly!  I couldn't believe what a joke that car was.  To top it off, his buddy in the RX7 saw the whole thing(this guy should have some respect for Fiero's by now, especially gold ones...hehe)  Now that I think about it, this CRX was probably not even an Si, so it wasn't a great kill...  BUT...  he was still a punk who thought his rusty Honda was a better car than my lowly Fiero.  Hardy har har.... or something to that effect.<P>-'87 GT, auto with a Crane Compucam.   <P><BR>ps-I think it's about time for a forum member to start a topic about the over-abundance of kill stories here lately!    <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">     <P>"My heroes are John Wayne, the Simpsons, and whoever canceled Full House/Bob Saget."||||reg||10
